1
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:09,370
You read the story on screen.

2
00:00:09,370 --> 00:00:12,720
The Earth says:

3
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:26,870
I have nutrients to nourish trees to grow. Without me, trees cannot live!

4
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:29,800
Water says:

5
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:40,670
If nutrients are not transported by water, can trees grow?

6
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,250
Air says:

7
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:52,550
Without air, all trees will wither.

8
00:00:52,550 --> 00:00:55,120
And Sunlight says:

9
00:00:55,120 --> 00:01:06,000
Even if trees have enough soil, water, air but lack sunlight, they cannot be green.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:17,100
Without green they cannot be called green trees!

11
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:29,970
Learn opinions and reasons of characters: Earth, Water, Air, Sunlight.

12
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:41,970
You connect each cell on the left with the suitable cell on the right.

13
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:54,070
Earth: Trees need Earth most: because soil has nutrients.

14
00:01:54,620 --> 00:02:06,000
Water: Trees need Water most: water transports nutrients.

15
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:17,870
Air: Trees need Air most: trees will wither without air.

16
00:02:18,370 --> 00:02:30,020
Sunlight: Trees need Sunlight most: trees cannot be green without sunlight.

17
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:39,070
You see the 4 characters express their own opinions.

18
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:46,470
Everyone affirms their role is important for trees.

19
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:53,100
Every opinion is correct because it gives a reasonable explanation.

20
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:59,350
Actually trees need soil, water, air and sunlight.

21
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:19,550
You have understood how to express opinions, defend your opinion, need to give reasons (reasons and evidence) for listeners to agree with you.

